    "Current production requests NSFileProtectionComplete for newly created snapshots directory and NSDataWritingAtomic|NSDataWritingFileProtectionComplete for every protected snapshot write.",
    "Current copied observer reads exact owned directory and file via attributesOfItemAtPath; a null dictionary, absent key, or unequal value each fails the same corresponding directory/file-protection stage.",
    "Apple Foundation documents NSFileProtectionKey values as NSString and attributesOfItemAtPath as returning nil on Objective-C error; SDK exposes these APIs/constants without a simulator-specific exclusion.",
    "Successful real simulator Foundation readback establishes only that runtime/volume metadata observation. It cannot establish physical iOS passcode, class-key eviction, locked-device inaccessibility, backup exclusion execution or Secure Enclave properties.",
    "Official SDK and current docs expose NSURLVolumeSupportsFileProtectionKey, iOS14+, read-only NSNumber capability. This has not been queried in this task and is not itself a protection guarantee.",
    "Counter-evidence: current Apple Platform Security describes Mac Apple-silicon Data Protection and opt-in stronger protection classes, so macOS hosting is not sufficient proof that metadata cannot exist.",
    "No fetched official page or inspected SDK header guarantees iOS26.5 Simulator NSFileManager directory/file protection-key readback or requires it to be absent. The exact native05 cause remains unestablished."
  ],
